# Where an early-access submission goes.
#
# `functions/api/early-access.ts` checks these in order and uses the first that
# is fully configured. With none of them set the endpoint returns 503 and the
# form says so — on purpose. A form that accepts a submission and drops it is a
# control that lies, and this is the wrong page for one.
#
# Locally these go in `.dev.vars` (wrangler reads that, not `.env`). In
# production they go on the Worker under Settings → Variables and Secrets,
# and take effect on the next deploy rather than the running one.

# --- Option 1: forward the JSON anywhere that accepts a POST ---------------
# A Zapier/Make hook, a Google Apps Script, an Airtable automation, your own
# endpoint. It receives { email, context, at, country }.
#
# `scripts/early-access-sheet.gs` is the receiver this was built for: it appends
# to a Google Sheet and emails you. Paste it into a Sheet's Apps Script, deploy
# it as a web app, and put the /exec URL here — README.md → "Wiring up the
# early-access form" has the steps and the two settings that are easy to miss.
#
# The URL is the only credential, and that is fine: it is read in the Worker,
# server-side, and never reaches a browser. Do not put it anywhere client-side.
EARLY_ACCESS_WEBHOOK_URL=

# --- Option 2: send it as an email instead --------------------------------
# Only reached when EARLY_ACCESS_WEBHOOK_URL is empty — the two destinations are
# alternatives, not a chain, and the webhook wins.
# All three are required together. `EARLY_ACCESS_FROM` must be on a domain
# verified in Resend; the submitted address is set as reply-to, so replying to
# the notification replies to the person.
RESEND_API_KEY=
EARLY_ACCESS_TO=
EARLY_ACCESS_FROM=

# --- The site's own URL ----------------------------------------------------
# Feeds canonical and OG URLs at build time. Unset, the build names
# https://portiadata.dev, which is what production wants.
SITE_URL=

# --- Where the launch film is served from ----------------------------------
# The encode is too big for Workers static assets (25 MiB a file) and lives in
# an R2 bucket on its own hostname. This is the URL that bucket answers on,
# with no trailing slash; the file name is in `src/content/film.yaml`.
#
# It is a build-time value: `PUBLIC_*` is inlined by Astro. Production's is
# committed in `.env.production`, because it is a public URL. Unset, the page
# falls back to `/film`, which is the gitignored `public/film/` the dev server
# plays and `pnpm film` fills.
PUBLIC_FILM_BASE=
